# oracle: fix gle with the equilibrium C matrix (GPL port of EXTRA-FIX/fix_gle.cpp), 64-water tip4p box, cut down to 40 steps.
# oracle-measured: thermo max rel 2.3e-9 (pe abs 1.2e-6); atoms max abs 8.1e-7 (fz), velocities abs 2.8e-10. The error is the pppm/tip4p base noise. Re-measured under Node 20 with a rolldown bundle: thermo rel 2.3e-9, atoms rel 4.5e-7 (same as Node 24). (Earlier run, before tightening; the current measurement is in the Measured line below.)
# oracle-inputs: data.h2o-smart smart.A
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 1.3e-13, atoms 3.5e-12.
units           real
atom_style      full
pair_style      lj/cut/tip4p/long 1 2 1 1 0.14714951 8
bond_style      class2
angle_style     harmonic
kspace_style    pppm/tip4p 0.0001
read_data       data.h2o-smart
pair_coeff      * 2  0.0     0.0
pair_coeff      1 1  0.1852  3.1589022
bond_coeff      1 0.9419 607.19354  -1388.6516 1852.577
angle_coeff     1 43.93  107.4
timestep        0.5
velocity        all create 300.0 1112 dist gaussian mom yes
fix             1 all gle 6 300.0 300.0 31415 smart.A
thermo_style    custom step temp pe ke etotal
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          10
run             40
